Partial scale-up grants whole replicas of multi-host worker groups.

KubeRay runs a multi-host worker group in whole replicas of numOfHosts pods and
rounds replicas down, but partial admission grants any pod count between the
baseline and the request. Kueue can charge 5 pods for a group whose replicas hold 2
pods each, while KubeRay creates 2 replicas, 4 pods. A scale-up from 4 pods
granted 5 counts as growth, so a slice is admitted at the size it replaces and
recreated again and again. The ungater also picks gated pods by name, which
starts one host of each of two replicas instead of one whole replica.

With ElasticJobsViaWorkloadSlicesWithPartialReplicaScaleUp on, the job reconciler
writes kueue.x-k8s.io/podset-count-steps with step numOfHosts for each multi-host
worker group of an elastic RayCluster, with PartialPreemption on or off. With
PartialPreemption on it also writes the multi-host floor, minReplicas x
numOfHosts. The scheduler's partial admission reduces step counts instead of pod
counts, so a grant is a whole number of steps, the baseline rounds up to a step,
and a scale-up must beat the baseline in whole steps. Steps of 1, a Workload
without the annotation, and the gate off leave admission unchanged. For a PodSet
with a step above 1 the ungater starts whole ray.io/worker-group-replica-name
groups, completing a started group first, starting a new group only once all
its pods exist, and never part of a group.

